The '''Nusu language''' is a [[Loloish language]] spoken by the [[Nu people]] of [[China]] and [[Myanmar]]. There are three dialects: Northern, Southern, and Central. The Central dialect of Miangu is the [[prestige dialect]] and is understood fairly well by speakers of other dialects.<ref name="e18"/>

Lama (2012) observes a sound change, *r- > Ø- from [[Proto-Loloish language|Proto-Loloish]], as a Nusoish innovation.

==Distribution==
The three Nusu dialects are spoken in the following locations (''Nusuzu Nusuyu Jianzhi'' 怒族怒苏语简志 1986).
